// Wren (M5 C12): the third playable kind, built on Aster's frame (`hero.figure.ron`, the same 64 joints of
// body, hands and face, so the heroine's clips cook for it as they do for her) and dressed to read apart
// from both at a glance: short dark hair with bangs and a high ponytail, a long charcoal coat open at the
// front whose tails fall to the calves at the sides and back, a high-collared teal shirt, dark trousers,
// boots to the knee, and a long staff in the right hand, banded in copper and tipped with a pale blue glow.
// Where Aster is a white jacket over a skirt and long silver hair with empty hands, Wren is a dark column
// with a staff across the frame.
//
// Six materials: skin, the face (face SDF masks baked from its normals; the expressions move it), hair,
// the coat (both sides drawn), the clothes and gear. 120 joints of its own, 121 with the model's root: 64
// for the body, hands and face, and 56 in spring chains (the coat's seven tails, the ponytail and five
// bangs), whose springs the VRM carries. The staff is skinned to `handslot.r`, as the Lancer's spear is,
// so the kind holds nothing else. All 18 of VRM 1.0's expression presets are morph targets on the face.
//
// `sapphire_pipeline gen-figures --specs tools/figures --out content` writes `content/combat/wren/`
// (`sapphire_pipeline::figure`); its sidecars and material documents are hand-written after Aster's.
// Metres, +Y up, facing +Z, its left toward +X, in a T-pose.
